-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 — the charge sheet.
--
-- The deployable surface of this row, after the pattern of
-- jl4/examples/legal/regcf/regcf-wizard.l4 in l4-ide: it re-implements no
-- law. Every offence module already exports its own ladders (`cheats`,
-- `offence under s 420`, …) and its own charge builders (`charge under s 420`,
-- …), because a ladder is drawn from the DECIDE that carries it and a wrapper
-- would draw as one box. What this module adds is the one question none of
-- them can answer alone:
--
--   given everything the officer has established, which sections are made out?
--
-- `Complaint` nests one facts record per offence family. An offence whose
-- facts the officer has not filled in is simply not made out — an empty record
-- has every element FALSE — so the router is total.
--
-- WHERE THE CRIMINAL BREACH OF TRUST CAPACITY IS READ FROM. Not from a new
-- field on `CBT Facts`, but from the NESTED RECORD `cbt-407-409.l4` declares:
-- `breach of trust` is an `Aggravated CBT Facts`, which carries the capacity
-- leaves of ss 407, 408 and 409 and nests the `CBT Facts` of s 405 inside
-- itself. So the s 406 row reaches through two records
-- (the complaint's breach of trust, then ITS breach of trust) while the three
-- aggravated rows read the outer one. That is the same nesting `Robbery Facts`
-- uses for its theft and extortion, and it keeps `CBT Facts` a record that can
-- still stand alone under a s 406 charge — which `cbt-405-406.l4`'s whole
-- Carl Elias Moses bench depends on.
--
-- ONE BREAKING CHANGE, for anything that supplies a `Complaint` by name: the
-- `breach of trust` field keeps its name but changes TYPE, from `CBT Facts` to
-- `Aggravated CBT Facts`.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `penal-code-general`
IMPORT `cheating-415-417-420`
IMPORT `theft-378-379`
IMPORT `extortion-383-384`
IMPORT `robbery-390-392`
IMPORT `misappropriation-403`
IMPORT `cbt-405-406`
IMPORT `cbt-407-409`
IMPORT `criminal-intimidation-503-506`
IMPORT `hurt-321-323A`

§ `Penal Code 1871 — the charge sheet`

@ref Criminal Procedure Code 2010 s 123 — one complaint, every offence this row encodes
-- `theft` and `theft in dwelling` each carry a `Theft Facts`, and nothing in
-- the type ties them together. A `Complaint` whose `theft in dwelling`'s nested
-- theft differed from its own `theft` could return s 380 without s 379 — which
-- s 380 itself forbids, theft being an element of theft in dwelling (Woon,
-- Essential Criminal Law ch. 8 p. 185). The row ALREADY has that shape for
-- robbery: `robbery` nests its own `Theft Facts` beside the `theft` field. It is
-- handled the same way here — every fixture below supplies the SAME named theft
-- record to both, and a reader adding one should do likewise. The alternative,
-- putting the five locus booleans loose on `Complaint` beside a single theft,
-- was rejected because it breaks this module's one rule: one nested facts
-- record per offence family, and no law re-implemented here.
DECLARE Complaint HAS
    cheating     IS A  `Cheating Facts`              @desc The deception, if any
    theft        IS A  `Theft Facts`                 @desc The taking, if any
    `theft in dwelling` IS A `Theft in Dwelling Facts` @desc The same taking with the place it happened in, if any — s 380 is the aggravated form, and its nested theft should be the same record as `theft`
    extortion    IS AN `Extortion Facts`             @desc The threat that got property, if any
    robbery      IS A  `Robbery Facts`               @desc The theft or extortion with violence, if any
    misappropriation  IS A `Misappropriation Facts` @desc The dishonest dealing with movable property that was never taken wrongfully, if any
    `breach of trust` IS AN `Aggravated CBT Facts`   @desc The entrustment, what became of the property, and the capacity the entrustment was made in, if any
    intimidation IS A  `Criminal Intimidation Facts` @desc The threat meant to alarm, if any
    hurt         IS A  `Hurt Facts`                  @desc The hurt caused, if any

-- WHERE THE "403" ROW GOES, AND WHY. s 403 and s 406 are one family — the two
-- offences of dishonestly dealing with property that was not wrongfully
-- obtained — and the router's stated rule is most serious first within each
-- family. s 406 carries up to 7 years, s 403 up to 2, so "403" follows "406".
-- Note that this is the seriousness rule and NOT a section-number rule: by
-- number 403 would come first. The list has never been in section order
-- anyway — "394" precedes "392", and "420" precedes "417" — so seriousness is
-- the only rule it follows.
--
-- NO IMPLICATION ROW IS OWED between "379" and "403". The 394/392/379 rows
-- overlap because s 390(1) says in terms that in all robbery there is either
-- theft or extortion, so a robbery IS a theft. Nothing of the kind ties theft
-- to misappropriation: they are alternatives, not a hierarchy. s 378
-- Illustration (g) says so from the theft side — the ring on the high road is
-- in nobody's possession, so there is no theft, "though he may commit criminal
-- misappropriation of property" — and the first fixture below makes that
-- boundary executable.
@export default The punishing sections of the Penal Code 1871 under which a charge can be framed on the facts of this complaint, most serious first within each family
GIVEN c IS A Complaint @desc Everything the investigation has established, one record per offence family
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`applicable charges` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`included if` (`offence under s 420` (c's cheating)) "420"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 417` (c's cheating)) "417"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 394` (c's robbery)) "394"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 392` (c's robbery)) "392"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 393` (c's robbery)) "393"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 380` (c's `theft in dwelling`)) "380"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 379` (c's theft)) "379"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 384` (c's extortion)) "384"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 409` (c's `breach of trust`)) "409"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 408` (c's `breach of trust`)) "408"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 407` (c's `breach of trust`)) "407"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 406` ((c's `breach of trust`)'s `breach of trust`)) "406"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 403` (c's misappropriation)) "403"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 506` (c's intimidation)) "506"),
        (`included if` (`offence under s 323A` (c's hurt)) "323A"))

§§ `Directives`

-- The locus records the complaints below need. Each nests the SAME theft record
-- its complaint gives the `theft` field, so the two can never disagree.

`no theft in dwelling` MEANS `Theft in Dwelling Facts` WITH
    theft                         IS `no theft`
    building                      IS FALSE
    tent                          IS FALSE
    vessel                        IS FALSE
    `as a human dwelling`         IS FALSE
    `for the custody of property` IS FALSE

-- Chen Weixiong Jerriek's robbery happened at the void deck of a block of
-- flats. A void deck is open on every side: it is not a building, tent or
-- vessel within s 380, so the theft there supports s 379 and not s 380.
`the handphone taken at the void deck` MEANS `Theft in Dwelling Facts` WITH
    theft                         IS `the handphone taken from Ng Juin Chye Joel`
    building                      IS FALSE
    tent                          IS FALSE
    vessel                        IS FALSE
    `as a human dwelling`         IS FALSE
    `for the custody of property` IS FALSE

`the handphone not taken, at the void deck` MEANS `Theft in Dwelling Facts` WITH
    theft                         IS `the handphone not taken from Ng Juin Chye Joel`
    building                      IS FALSE
    tent                          IS FALSE
    vessel                        IS FALSE
    `as a human dwelling`         IS FALSE
    `for the custody of property` IS FALSE

-- The Lewis Christine facts alone: both cheating sections, nothing else.
`Lewis Christine's complaint` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- Chen Weixiong Jerriek: the robbery, with the hurt the s 394 charges alleged.
`Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `the handphone taken from Ng Juin Chye Joel`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `the handphone taken at the void deck`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- The same encounter, one step short: the taking never happened, so s 392 and
-- s 379 both drop out and s 393 takes their place. s 394 is unmoved, because
-- it reaches an attempt in terms.
`Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint, the attempt` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `the handphone not taken from Ng Juin Chye Joel`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `the handphone not taken, at the void deck`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, the attempt`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- THE THEFT / MISAPPROPRIATION BOUNDARY, MADE EXECUTABLE. s 378 Illustration
-- (g) and s 403 Explanation 2 Illustration (f) are the same ring: taking it is
-- no theft, because it was in nobody's possession and there was nothing to take
-- it out of; selling it at once without looking for the owner is an offence
-- under s 403. The theft side is `no theft` — the all-FALSE record, which is
-- the honest answer when the section's every element is absent — and the router
-- returns the one section that does lie.
`the ring found on the high road` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `the ring sold at once`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- The same finding, one step short of the offence: s 403 Explanation 2
-- Illustration (a), the dollar picked up on the high road. No section lies at
-- all, which is the vacuity control this router did not previously have — until
-- now every assertion below named at least one section, so a router that
-- over-reported would have been caught but one that reported spuriously on
-- empty facts would not.
`the dollar found on the high road` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `the dollar on the high road`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- Shop theft, the case Woon calls by far the most common version of theft: the
-- router lists s 380 and s 379 on the same taking, the 7-year section first.
-- Woon, Essential Criminal Law ch. 8 p. 185, records that it is not clear from
-- the SPF Annual Crime Brief 2022 which of the two shop theft is prosecuted
-- under, and that cases may straddle both — charged under s 380, reduced to
-- s 379 on a plea of guilt. Both rows firing is that straddle.
`Tan Mei Ling's complaint` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `Tan Mei Ling`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `Tan Mei Ling, in the supermarket`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- The same taking at an open-air stall: s 379 alone. This is the row that would
-- fail if the 380 row ever stopped reading the locus.
`Tan Mei Ling's complaint, in the open` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `Tan Mei Ling`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `Tan Mei Ling, in the open`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- The aggravated criminal breach of trust family, on the Carl Elias Moses
-- entrustment as the court said it should have been pleaded. The capacity is
-- supposed, not reported — see cbt-407-409.l4's header.
`the employee's complaint` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

`the director's complaint` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

-- The same employee, entrusted in a private capacity instead. s 408 drops out
-- and s 406 alone remains — eight years of maximum sentence turning on one
-- leaf, which is why the router now asks the question at all.
`the employee's complaint, not entrusted as an employee` MEANS Complaint WITH
    cheating          IS `Lewis Christine, no deception`
    theft             IS `no theft`
    `theft in dwelling` IS `no theft in dwelling`
    extortion         IS `no extortion`
    robbery           IS `Chen Weixiong Jerriek, no aggravation`
    misappropriation  IS `no misappropriation`
    `breach of trust` IS `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`
    intimidation      IS `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were`
    hurt              IS `Ang Boon Han, the hurt intended was grievous`

#EVAL `applicable charges` `Lewis Christine's complaint`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint, the attempt`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `Tan Mei Ling's complaint`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `Tan Mei Ling's complaint, in the open`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `the employee's complaint`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `the director's complaint`
#EVAL `applicable charges` `the employee's complaint, not entrusted as an employee`

-- s 420 implies s 417: the router lists both, aggravated first
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `Lewis Christine's complaint` EQUALS LIST "420", "417"
-- a robbery is also a theft (s 390(1)): s 394, s 392 and s 379 all lie
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint` EQUALS LIST "394", "392", "379"
-- an attempted robbery: s 394 still lies (its own words reach an attempt),
-- s 393 replaces s 392, and the theft charge goes with the completed taking
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `Chen Weixiong Jerriek's complaint, the attempt` EQUALS LIST "394", "393"
-- shop theft: the aggravated section first, the simple one under it
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `Tan Mei Ling's complaint` EQUALS LIST "380", "379"
-- the same taking in the open: s 380 drops out and s 379 stands alone
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `Tan Mei Ling's complaint, in the open` EQUALS LIST "379"
-- the ring on the high road: no theft lies, s 403 does, and the router says so
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `the ring found on the high road` EQUALS LIST "403"
-- the dollar picked up: nothing lies anywhere
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `the dollar found on the high road` EQUALS EMPTY

-- Criminal breach of trust: the aggravated section first, then s 406, which
-- every one of them is built on and which therefore always accompanies them.
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `the employee's complaint` EQUALS LIST "408", "406"
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `the director's complaint` EQUALS LIST "409", "406"
-- the capacity withdrawn: the family collapses to the section it is built on
#ASSERT `applicable charges` `the employee's complaint, not entrusted as an employee` EQUALS LIST "406"
